# Build environment of the desktop application (Windows, CPU-only, Python 3.12): the packages chosen by hand.
#
# requirements.txt is generated from this file by packaging\pin.ps1. It pins every package, including
# indirect ones, to an exact version and file checksum, so a build always uses the same, verified files.
# The versions are those of uv.lock, so the packaged application runs the same libraries as the project
# environment; only PyTorch differs in being the CPU build from PyTorch's own package index.
#
# After changing a version here or in uv.lock, run:  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File packaging\pin.ps1

